            <ArticleTitle>[Eye pain from an otorhinolaryngology perspective].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1127-33</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1007/s00347-011-2397-7</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Ocular and orbital pain are regularly occurring symptoms in ophthalmological clinics and therefore require differentiated clinical diagnostics in order to be able to offer efficient therapy options. An interdisciplinary approach is necessary due to the plenitude of possible causes, these also including otolaryngology diseases because of the anatomical proximity of nasal sinuses and orbital cavities. This paper aims to give an overview of otorhinolaryngological diseases which must be taken into account in the context of ocular and orbital pain.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
